# Auth & session

## Stack
- NextAuth Credentials → Laravel `POST /auth/login` → Sanctum `access_token`
- Token lives in NextAuth JWT (`accessToken`, `accessTokenExpiresAt`, `role`)
- Client API calls: pass Bearer via `useAuthClient()` / `session.accessToken`

## Session validity
- Treat as logged in only if `status === "authenticated"` **and** `session.accessToken` exists **and** no `session.error` (e.g. `AccessTokenExpired`)
- Middleware already guards `/account`, `/dashboard`, `/profile`, `/admin` — don't reimplement redirects inconsistently
- `/admin` requires `role === "superadmin"`; this frontend has little/no admin UI

## Auth pages
- Login/register: Indonesian copy; use `SITE_NAME` from site-config
- Respect `callbackUrl` query after login
- If already valid session on `/auth/*`, redirect away (middleware + page checks)
- Register UI may collect phone; API currently expects `name`, `email`, `password`, `password_confirmation`

## Account area
- Dashboard / balance / settings / API keys need Bearer token
- Balance payment on order page depends on same session
- On API 401 with Bearer: use client sign-out flow (avoid hard redirect cookie loops)

## Roles
- Display via `roleLabel()` in `src/lib/role.ts`: `member` | `superadmin`
- Do not add OAuth (Google/Facebook) unless backend supports it — UI icons alone are not enough
